<title>USA: Electric Boat says lays off 539.</title>
<headline>Electric Boat says lays off 539.</headline>
<dateline>GROTON, Conn. 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Submarine maker Electric Boat Corp, a unit of General Dynamics Corp, said Monday it laid off 539 employees because of a shrinking work load.</p>
<p>The layoffs will take effect April 19, Electric Boat said in a statement.</p>
<p>Nearly all of the laid off employees worked at the Groton shipyard in production or support jobs.</p>
<p>After the layoffs, the company's Groton workforce will be about 8,500, Electric Boat spokesman Neil Ruenzel told Reuters.</p>
<p>Ruenzel said last week the company expected to announce layoffs of up to 1,500 employees this year, but he gave no time frame.</p>
<p>Jobs have declined steadily since 1991 because orders are falling with the end of the Cold War.</p>
<p>((--Hartford newsroom (860) 727-0224))</p>
